In `checkIfIsAvailable`, the working-hours validation computes both `start` and `end` from `slotStartTime`:
```ts
const start = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
const end = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
if (start < workingHour.startTime || end > workingHour.endTime) return true;
```
Because `end` is not based on `slotEndTime`, a slot that starts within working hours but extends past `workingHour.endTime` will not be rejected (since `end === start`). This matches the finding’s described mechanism, and this branch is explicitly used only when no date over

